WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:04.770
Littlefinger, like most characters in the
later seasons, was utterly demolished by David

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.819
and Dan’s incompetent writing.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:11.070
So for this video, I want to try my best to
fix his character and to give him a much better

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.299
resolution.

00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:16.110
Instead of the abysmal train wreck of an ending
he got in season 7.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:20.130
The first thing we need to do is assess what
made Littlefinger so great to begin with,

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.540
so we can better understand why he was lacking
in the later seasons.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:28.310
And to me, by far Littlefingers best aspect
is that he plays into one of the show’s

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.609
strengths which is the rich mystery of conspiracy.

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:35.989
Littlefinger’s deceptive usage of scheming
and backstabbing is so alluring because he

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:39.900
entangles characters in a thick mud of conflict
that drowns them.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.239
To me, it’s more intriguing than something
like dueling because there’s an air of unpredictability

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:46.170
as to what Littlefinger will do.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:50.620
We understand his motives, but the actions
he takes to fulfill them is always captivating

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.039
to watch unravel.

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:56.699
This is exemplified the most in season 1 where
Littlefinger quite literally kickstarts the

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:59.379
entire conflict of the series.

00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:02.899
Without Littlefinger there really wouldn’t
be a show because think about it.

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:06.970
Littlefinger simultaneously manipulates Lysa
Arryn to poison her husband Jon Arryn, which

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:11.409
in turn brings the Starks into the fold, and
he hires an assassin to kill Bran under the

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:13.729
guise that it was the Lannisters who did it.

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:18.090
Littlefinger flat out orchestrates an entire
war in the realm so that he can profit by

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.479
helping each side.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:23.970
I feel like by that alone Littlefinger is
the most evil character in the entire show

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.710
and most people normally point to Ramsay or
Joffrey.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.850
The sheer impact that this character has is
arguably the biggest right behind Dany’s

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.930
mad queen arc and the Night King.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.450
You can argue that other villains like Tywin
and Joffrey are more deadly, but they were

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.770
spurred into doing heinous actions because
of Littlefinger.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:43.780
Like the red wedding and Tywin destroying
the riverlands wouldn’t be a thing without

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:44.780
Petyr.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:48.530
What they did in the show comes nowhere near
as close to the massive amount of damage that

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.719
Littlefinger has done to Westeros.

00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:55.240
He is the mastermind of most major events
and he’s the one that’s paving the way

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.119
for this engrossing conflict.

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:01.460
I’m not going to go very in depth about
what makes Littlefinger so great since this

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:05.900
video is after all about fixing him and not
analyzing his greatness.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:11.090
But to put simply he has a large impact, the
very nature of his character is very mysterious

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:15.599
and alluring, and the way in which he overcomes
his enemies and furthers his position is fueled

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:17.489
with high intelligence.

00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:21.879
Making every scene he’s in very entertaining
and you’re constantly excited to see what

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:22.880
he’s up to.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:29.360
Now in the later seasons, all of these aspects
about Littlefinger are severely downgraded.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.880
Myself and other channels have been pretty
vocal about Littlefinger’s handling in the

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.920
later seasons, but I feel like I’ve seen
a common sentiment that Littlefinger was only

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.050
ruined in his final season.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.900
Which I completely disagree with.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.420
Or some people have even argued that his ending
was actually fine.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:48.040
So for this section of the video we are going
to identify where everything went wrong with

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:52.790
Littlefinger and how he was downgraded so
much so I can then propose fixes to these

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:53.790
problems.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:57.920
Funnily enough, the most pressing issue isn’t
actually Littlefinger’s death, but the exact

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.680
moment in which he betrays Sansa by handing
her over to the Boltons.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.130
There’s a lot to dive into here and first
let’s try to understand Littlefinger’s

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.940
plan for season 5 because it’s very confounding.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:14.709
So Littlefinger in an attempt to ally himself
with the Bolton’s gives Sansa over to them,

00:03:14.709 --> 00:03:19.050
and he does this because he’s betting that
Stannis will win and liberate Winterfell.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:23.319
His reasoning for giving Sansa over is that
since she’ll be at Winterfell already, Stannis

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:25.420
will then make her warden of the north.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.290
However, that immediately doesn’t make sense
and is an extremely convoluted way to become

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.290
warden of the north.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.319
Instead, he could simply ally the Vale with
Stannis and in exchange for helping, Sansa

00:03:35.319 --> 00:03:36.950
becomes Warden of the North.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:41.019
However, this isn’t actually Littlefinger’s
plan because he then gets summoned to talk

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:44.010
to Cersei and hatches an alternate plot with
her.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:48.260
There he pitches a plan where he wants Cersei
to send an army of Lannisters to attack Stannis’

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.890
army after they win while they’re recovering.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:56.450
She says no for obvious reasons, and Littlefinger
also proposes himself to attack with the Vale,

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:59.970
and in return, he wants to become Warden of
the North.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:04.130
Although Cersei then says that she wants Sansa’s
head so I guess that immediately invalidates

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:08.810
this entire pitch because I assume Littlefinger
is lying when he says yes.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.599
Given that he’s in love with Sansa, or maybe
he’s lying about that, I don’t even know

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:13.599
anymore.

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:17.600
I’d make the case that he does love Sansa,
and that kind of aspect about his character

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.590
is truly his constant.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:24.570
But after this point, Littlefinger literally
disappears from the remainder of season 5.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.320
This scene happens during episode 6 by the
way.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:32.020
So Littlefinger is MIA for a long time and
I presume that he had no intentions of sending

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:36.120
the Vale to Winterfell since that would be
a major commitment, and he’d have to be

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:39.169
nearby to actually attack Stannis after he
won.

00:04:39.169 --> 00:04:43.150
Along with him probably alienating the entirety
of the North by doing that.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:48.130
So yeah, there’s a lot to unpack here from
how devoid of logic and unnecessarily complicated

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.930
this entire plan is.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:53.960
Addressing the scene with Cersei first, I
assume Littlefinger was shooting for a hail

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:58.220
mary scenario in which the Lannisters would
take out the victor and establish him as Warden

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.600
of the North or something.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.680
However, that would compromise Sansa, so that
wouldn’t make any sense.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.820
This now makes me think that this entire scene
was just Littlefinger lying to Cersei to appease

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.810
her and if that was the case then that was
unnecessary.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:15.229
Cersei is eventually going to figure out that
Littlefinger is working against her, so he

00:05:15.229 --> 00:05:18.630
may as well just ignore Cersei and accept
her as an enemy.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:23.310
Why bother going all the way down to Kingslanding
from Winterfell just to lie to her and gain

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.960
practically nothing?

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.180
On top of the fact that Littlefinger publicly
gave Sansa to the Boltons at Winterfell so

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:34.069
there is a risk in him going to Kingslanding
because of a possibility that Cersei was informed

00:05:34.069 --> 00:05:35.120
about that.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.729
Like she coincidentally summons him right
after he shows up in Winterfell with Sansa.

00:05:39.729 --> 00:05:42.530
Hmmmm I wonder what she would want to talk
about.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:47.169
So this entire scene with Cersei feels pointless,
especially since this set-up leads absolutely

00:05:47.169 --> 00:05:48.169
nowhere.

00:05:48.169 --> 00:06:10.770
Along with it making Littlefinger's plan very
confusing.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:14.569
Now let's go back to Littlefinger giving Sansa
to the Boltons and assume that his initial

00:06:14.569 --> 00:06:19.190
plan was betting on Stannis to win and to
establish Sansa as Warden of the North.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:23.370
Like before, there’s a much better plan
available that achieves this same goal in

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:24.870
allying with Stannis.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.830
Which doesn’t alienate Sansa.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.590
That just seems like the most logical approach
to the situation.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:35.060
Instead, Littlefinger throws away that which
he loves the most to THE BOLTONS.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.930
In season 6, Littlefinger claims that he didn’t
know that Ramsay would be that unhinged and

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:46.780
goes the route of ignorance.

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:54.210
Like he’s not lying and genuinely didn’t
know anything about Ramsay.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:07:00.289
However, Littlefinger as a character prides
himself on being extremely well informed and

00:07:00.289 --> 00:07:04.660
would never act on a plan if there was a variable
that was a major question mark to him.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:08.910
As an example, Littlefinger flat out kills
Dontas Hollard because he didn’t trust him

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.440
to keep his mouth shut.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:14.120
Since his future allegiance was a question
mark, he decided that killing him would be

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.460
a permanent solution to that problem.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:21.460
So giving Sansa away to an unknown figure,
whose the son of a ruthless father who massacred

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.810
her entire family is absolutely wild.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.240
I feel like it would be safe to assume that
Ramsey would at least be somewhat like his

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.260
father and if not even crazier.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:36.900
Although, it does seem like Roose Bolton is
mostly well mannered, but my point still stands.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:56.060
In the world of 

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:00.620
Game of Thrones with so many crazy lords,
it’s inherently a huge gamble to give Sansa

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:05.220
away to a random lord within a house that
is notorious for flaying people I might add.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.449
That’s by far the most ridiculous thing
that Littlefinger does that immediately compromises

00:08:09.449 --> 00:08:10.449
his character.

00:08:10.449 --> 00:08:15.000
Littlefinger’s extremely convoluted and
nonsensical plan for this season is like trying

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.210
to navigate a complex web of hardened cum.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:21.979
It feels like it was made by someone who doesn’t
understand the character at all because it

00:08:21.979 --> 00:08:23.340
reeks of stupidity.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:26.970
It’s very clear that David and Dan were
trying to imitate what Littlefinger would

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:30.550
act like given that they ran out of source
material for him.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:34.289
From here, we have season 6 which essentially
downgrades Littlefinger’s presence in the

00:08:34.289 --> 00:08:35.289
show.

00:08:35.289 --> 00:08:38.909
It mostly feels like David and Dan gave up
doing anything with the character and pretty

00:08:38.909 --> 00:08:43.130
much relegated him to trying to appease Sansa
for all of season 6.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:46.529
Because rightfully so, his actions in season
5 were baffling.

00:08:46.529 --> 00:08:51.000
And not in a way that you could understand
the fault, but in a contrived way in which

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.300
David and Dan bent the character into a direction
that made him very dumb.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:09:00.250
This leads to season 7 where yet again, Littlefinger
has a completely batshit insane plan of trying

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.190
to get Sansa to kill Arya.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:07.399
Now, Littlefinger is a character that naturally
has to take great risks to further his position.

00:09:07.399 --> 00:09:12.180
Like orchestrating the entire conflict in
season 1 and conspiring to kill Joffrey.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:16.740
However, the difference between those two
examples and his season 7 plot is that they

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.490
are much more calculated and safe.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:24.400
He only conspires with people he trusts to
stay quiet and his plans are normally air

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.400
tight.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:29.880
In season 7, he’s basically trying to convince
Sansa that Arya wants to kill her and become

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.510
Lady of Winterfell.

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:34.370
Which this is insane for a couple reasons.

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:39.250
Firstly and most importantly, Arya notoriously
did not want to be a lady and she wanted to

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.260
be a warrior.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.360
This was very out in the open and Sansa even
hated her for that and wished Arya would be

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:45.750
more like a lady.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:50.089
Since Arya’s more rambunctious personality
would oftentimes compromise Sansa’s happiness.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:53.910
I started reading the books recently and they
go much more in depth about this while the

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.920
show partially shows this.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.650
Sansa should immediately understand Arya’s
core wants in life and realize that Littlefinger’s

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:03.370
claim that she wants to be Lady of Winterfell
is bullshit.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:07.810
I know people can change through life, but
Arya is still very much a warrior and if Sansa

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:12.380
was really suspicious of this she could simply
talk to her sister and try to determine what

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.640
her goals are.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:18.720
Instead of taking Littlefinger’s advice,
someone she knows she can’t trust.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:22.800
Another issue that doesn’t directly involve
Littlefinger as a character, is the contrivance

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.320
of this conflict.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:28.700
David and Dan essentially bend Arya’s character
into being unrealistically cold and crazy

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.930
towards her sister when that shouldn’t be
the case.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:36.750
Like Arya gets really mad at Sansa for writing
a letter to Rob to bend the knee to Joffrey,

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:40.010
but she was literally held prisoner and was
forced to do that.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:44.510
Even Robb and his council immediately identified
the letter as being bullshit and for some

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.170
reason Arya goes crazy about this.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:51.170
As if Sansa betrayed her house and this piece
of information will destroy everything when

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.410
it shouldn’t.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:55.670
She even goes as far to act like she’s about
to kill her sister.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:59.589
I feel like this is just an obvious example
of David and Dan exaggerating the amount of

00:10:59.589 --> 00:11:03.560
anger Arya would feel here to create a false
sense of conflict.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:07.920
Not even mentioning the fact that Sansa could
literally go to Bran for counsel about this

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:10.180
since he told her he knows everything.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:14.420
Or Bran being the one to go to his sisters
and telling them about Littlefinger’s conspiracies

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:17.610
that he literally confirms to Littlefinger’s
face.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:21.470
The fact that Littlefinger just brushes off
the notion that Bran knows about his secret

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:24.370
conversation with Varys is hilarious.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:28.579
Bran is clearly indicating to Littlefinger
that he knows what he’s done in the past,

00:11:28.579 --> 00:11:34.339
but Littlefinger for whatever reason, is completely
unphased by this and carries on with his ridiculous

00:11:34.339 --> 00:11:35.339
plan.

00:11:35.339 --> 00:11:38.610
These are the reasons why Littlefinger was
ruined and people generally focus solely on

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:43.720
his death scene as being dumb, but in reality,
it’s everything that leads up to this point.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:47.959
Littlefinger’s terrible and ruined fate
was fully sealed by this point and his death

00:11:47.959 --> 00:11:51.899
essentially evokes no emotion from how ruined
he was.

00:11:51.899 --> 00:11:55.290
From here, I’m going to go into two parts
in trying to fix his character.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.649
The first one being fixing everything within
seasons 5 through 7.

00:11:58.649 --> 00:12:02.130
And then the second part will be pitching
an alternative path for the character that

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:04.370
would make more sense and would better suit
him.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:08.550
So tackling the season 5 debacle of giving
Sansa away to the Boltons, I think the most

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:11.600
simple change would be to be more faithful
to the books.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.120
In the books, there’s a character that is
friends with Sansa named Jeyne Poole that

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.720
the Lannisters send claiming she’s Arya
Stark.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:21.589
In the show, Littlefinger can do this and
they could simply say he had her stashed away

00:12:21.589 --> 00:12:24.290
in his whorehouse and has been working there.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:28.240
Most of the people currently occupying Winterfell
don’t know what Arya looks like so it’s

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.450
actually a good plan.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:33.150
And even if Jeyne is questioned about anything,
she would know the answers given her close

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:34.880
relationship with Sansa.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:39.500
The only people that would know her true identity
would maybe be some Stark loyalists and Theon

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.500
Greyjoy.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:44.310
Which I think this would make an interesting
dynamic in Theon trying to keep the identity

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:46.290
of Jeyne Poole a secret.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:50.690
Essentially adding a more complex layer to
Theon in having to hide information from Ramsay.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:55.100
Or maybe he even has to kill people who suspect
her identity is fake to protect her.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:59.170
I admittedly haven’t gotten to this point
yet in the books, but it already makes significantly

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.620
more sense than what David and Dan chose to
do.

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:06.029
And I feel like the main reason why David
and Dan chose to put Sansa Stark in her place

00:13:06.029 --> 00:13:09.180
is because they thought it would make this
subplot more dramatic.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:12.839
Which I would disagree because we still have
Theon as a point of view character within

00:13:12.839 --> 00:13:17.959
Winterfell and like the show, this could be
the event that causes Theon to defect and

00:13:17.959 --> 00:13:19.800
save Jeyne from Ramsay’s torture.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:23.710
There’s a much more complex plot with Mance
Rayder going to Winterfell to save Jeyne in

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:27.120
the books, but we physically wouldn’t be
able to do that since Mance is dead in the

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:28.120
show.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:31.450
And I don’t think it would be necessary
and Theon could come up with a smart plan

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:32.779
to get Jeyne out.

00:13:32.779 --> 00:13:37.959
Overall, this would be more logical from Littlefinger's
perspective because he both gets to keep Sansa

00:13:37.959 --> 00:13:42.180
to himself and loyal to him, while also making
an ally with the boltons.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:46.610
That and his plan of going to Cersei and getting
her to attack whoever the victor is wouldn’t

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:49.260
compromise Sansa because it would be Jeyne
instead.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:51.170
Assuming he still wanted to do that.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:54.750
This seems like such a low hanging fruit of
a fix that it just makes me think that David

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:58.640
and Dan didn’t really care about overall
logic and only wanted to raise the drama by

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:00.149
turning Jeyne into Sansa.

00:14:00.149 --> 00:14:04.450
They severely misunderstood Littlefinger as
a character because even George RR.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:07.250
Martin said that Littlefinger would never
betray Sansa.

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:12.170
And the sad thing is, if it wasn’t for Bran,
Sansa probably would have been manipulated

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:14.540
into killing Arya like a dumbass.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.940
Which just seems so crazy to me that she still
listens to Littlefinger in season 7.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:23.300
So that would be an easy fix to the biggest
problem in season 5 and I would also propose

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:27.839
a change in which the conflict within the
Eyrie, where the lords don’t trust Littlefinger,

00:14:27.839 --> 00:14:29.649
to not be resolved so quickly.

00:14:29.649 --> 00:14:33.290
I think it would be more interesting to have
at least one or two lords in the Vale to not

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.060
trust Sansa’s testimony.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:39.190
Or maybe there’s a small hole in Sansa’s
testimony that one of the Lord notices and

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:40.850
investigates further.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:44.459
Because currently in the Vale, there’s no
conflict for Littlefinger to overcome after

00:14:44.459 --> 00:14:45.459
this trial.

00:14:45.459 --> 00:14:49.339
Instead, I feel like it would be a more engaging
narrative if Littlefinger had to covertly

00:14:49.339 --> 00:14:52.110
deal with one of these lords and kill them.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:56.959
Essentially utilizing his primary way of overcoming
conflict of scheming and conspiracy.

00:14:56.959 --> 00:15:01.820
This could pad out some time within season
5 and 6 because besides the Winterfell plot,

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:03.350
Littlefinger has nothing to do.

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:05.990
He literally vanishes from the narrative.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:09.420
Littlefinger is clearly making enemies in
the Vale like him flat out threatening to

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:10.420
kill Lord Royce.

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:15.089
You could easily develop a plot thread from
there in which Lord Royce tries to exact revenge

00:15:15.089 --> 00:15:17.070
on Petyr through his own plan.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:21.209
But maybe Petyr makes short work of Lord Royce
because he’s inexperienced at playing dirty

00:15:21.209 --> 00:15:23.860
and coming up with a plot to get Littlefinger
killed.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:27.779
Instead, Royce kind of just rolls over and
easily submits to Littlefinger when I feel

00:15:27.779 --> 00:15:32.190
like this type of character would try to rebel
out of pure spite for Littlefinger’s dirtiness

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:34.090
and dishonorable nature.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:38.480
This again would give Littlefinger something
to do in season 6 because now that he wouldn’t

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.800
have alienated Sansa, there’ll have to be
new material for the character.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:45.860
And I’m not sure if the books really cover
this far for him so this would essentially

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:50.930
be going into unknown territory for his character
that wouldn’t be derived from source material.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:54.910
Because I obviously wouldn’t even try to
fix his season 7 plot and would rather that

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.779
be removed entirely.

00:15:56.779 --> 00:16:00.220
This is essentially going into the second
part of fixing his character in proposing

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:02.620
a different direction and resolution for Littlefinger.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:07.220
I’d argue that Littlefinger is the most
important villain in the entire show because

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:09.180
he’s the mastermind of everything.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:13.490
So having him still be relevant in a major
way I think would be important for his character

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.380
and would be faithful to him.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:19.670
Instead of utterly downgrading him to being
a Sansa simp and kissing her toes all the

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:20.670
time.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:24.250
I think a longer term goal for Littlefinger
that reshapes the show would be more interesting.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.070
While also being more in character for him.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:31.529
For this pitch, since I want Littlefinger
to make a great impact like the earlier seasons,

00:16:31.529 --> 00:16:34.500
that means I need to alter the final seasons
of the show.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:38.899
So for season 7 I’m going to solely focus
the narrative on Dany’s war with Cersei

00:16:38.899 --> 00:16:42.470
and then season 8 primarily dealing with the
Night King and the mad queen arc.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:45.910
Or there could even be a season 9 where we
split the Night King and the mad queen arc,

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.829
but it doesn’t need to be that detailed.

00:16:47.829 --> 00:16:51.550
My pitch would be after dealing with Lord
Royce and making sure his grasp on the Vale

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:55.269
is fully secured, Littlefinger starts conspiring
against Cersei.

00:16:55.269 --> 00:16:59.550
In the hopes that by betraying her, Dany will
honor his loyalty by granting him more power

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:00.950
and wealth.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:05.110
Some of the details here could be Littlefinger
killing characters in Kingslanding like maybe

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:06.910
Qyburn to destabilize the kingdom.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:11.100
That could be a factor as to why the scorpions
were so incompetent in season 8.

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:15.120
Qyburn could have possibly been working on
designs and Littlefinger kills him during

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:19.610
the process, and Cersei half haphazardly implements
them even though they weren’t finished.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:24.250
That’s just an example of something Littlefinger
could do that simultaneously solves some problems

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.650
in season 8.

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:29.410
One of the other ones being Qyburn’s awkward
and strangely funny death scene.

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:33.049
Or you could also save Kevan Lannister’s
character from being killed in the great sept

00:17:33.049 --> 00:17:37.770
explosion and have Littlefinger kill him in
an attempt to weaken the Lannister army.

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:41.520
Because when you think of the sept explosion
you probably forgot that Kevan was even there

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:45.299
from how many other character deaths overshadowed
his.

00:17:45.299 --> 00:17:49.390
So there’s a lot of opportunities for Littlefinger
to cause chaos behind the scenes and in the

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:54.660
process he could be offering up intel to Cersei
to make her not suspect him as being a spy.

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:58.500
After Cersei inevitably loses to Daenerys,
this leaves both the Mad Queen arc and the

00:17:58.500 --> 00:17:59.990
Night King conflict.

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:03.140
Both of which I’d still have Littlefinger
playing a major part.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:06.241
So this depends on what should come first
narratively because I feel like the Night

00:18:06.241 --> 00:18:10.929
King conflict should be the final conflict,
but narratively it feels more natural for

00:18:10.929 --> 00:18:13.130
it to happen before the mad queen arc.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:17.220
So I’ll do a similar structure of season
8’s plot, but obviously different.

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:21.400
I won’t go into that much detail and will
only focus on what Littlefinger does.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:25.120
After Cersei's defeat and Littlefinger once
again is awarded for his scheming, I would

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:30.539
expect Jon Snow or most likely Varys to convince
Dany to exile Littlefinger from Kingslanding

00:18:30.539 --> 00:18:32.700
due to his history of being a snake.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:34.940
He is not to be trusted.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:38.470
Naturally this would upset Littlefinger and
this may be a major departure from where the

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:42.900
show went, but I think it would be really
interesting if Littlefinger got control of

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:44.510
the Horn of Winter.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:48.250
Given that the show actually shows it in season
2 when the Nights Watch was at the Fist of

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:49.250
the First Men.

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:53.309
If you don’t know what the Horn of Winter
is, it’s rumored that the Horn, if blown,

00:18:53.309 --> 00:18:55.350
will be able to bring down the wall.

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:58.780
It technically doesn’t come back up again
in the show, but maybe Littlefinger hears

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:03.220
rumors about it being brought to Castle Black
and he hatches a plan to steal it.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:07.510
The way in which he hears about it could possibly
be through him eavesdropping on a conversation

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:10.270
with Tormund and Jon where they discuss the
Horn.

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:12.560
The wildlings apparently know about it through
reputation.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:16.810
It would make sense that finding the Horn
would be a major goal for Jon so that no one

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:19.809
has the power of destroying the wall and unleashing
the Night King.

00:19:19.809 --> 00:19:23.980
So this would essentially enact a race between
these two parties in trying to get to the

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:24.980
horn first.

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:28.429
In stealing the Horn of Winter, Littlefinger
would probably replace it with a fake and

00:19:28.429 --> 00:19:30.919
at the end of an episode he’ll blow the
horn.

00:19:30.919 --> 00:19:35.100
A cool moment could be Jon getting to the
Horn and then Tormund says that it’s a fake,

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:37.630
cutting to Littlefinger bringing down the
wall.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:39.890
Thus unleashing chaos into the realm.

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:43.530
This would essentially act as Littlefinger
getting revenge on the lords in Kingslanding

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:48.210
and he will probably try to profit in some
way from the misery caused by the Night King.

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:51.980
I think this thematically stays true to Littlefinger’s
character because he wants to cripple the

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:54.539
realm and benefit off of its misery.

00:19:54.539 --> 00:19:58.120
Which is what he did in the earlier seasons
and it would make sense for this to remain

00:19:58.120 --> 00:19:59.560
being the case.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:03.650
Along with the fact that Littlefinger would
probably be the only one to actually want

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:05.429
this chaos to unfold.

00:20:05.429 --> 00:20:10.240
I think in the books Euron is also a possibility,
but the tame and destroyed rendition of him

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:12.890
would not make sense for that to happen in
the show.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:16.740
So by making it to where Littlefinger brings
down the wall, this would also solve the major

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:21.680
issue in season 7 where Tyrion comes up with
the atrocious plan of kidnapping a wight.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:26.340
That entire plot was extremely contrived because
even if Cersei believed them she still probably

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:27.559
wouldn’t help them.

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:31.840
Which is what happens and this plot only exists
to deliver a dragon to the Night King.

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:36.030
However, with my pitch, I think it would be
much better to make it a character motivated

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:40.530
decision that doesn’t compromise the intellect
of a bunch of characters.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:43.840
From this point in the story, I think the
most logical path for Littlefinger would be

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:46.610
to retreat to the Vale and ride out the storm.

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:50.750
To not fully upset the lords, he might allow
some of his troops to help out in the overall

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.440
fight, but I’d find it hard to imagine that
he’ll help out completely.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:57.140
Or maybe he’ll try to lie about his infantry
numbers.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:01.220
After the heroes inevitably defeat the Night
King, this will now lead us to the Mad Queen

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:02.220
arc.

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:06.330
Now for this, I think a much cooler development
would be for Sansa to still doubt Dany and

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:11.250
overall dislike her, but to build up that
distrust over the seasons instead of it happening

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.580
instantly.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:18.460
Then because of this, Sansa goes to Littlefinger
to conspire with her in taking down Daenerys.

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:23.340
In a way, Sansa and Littlefinger help orchestrate
the Mad Queen arc into existence by doing

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:26.310
different things like assassinating her closest
friends.

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:31.159
Maybe they could even convince Arya into doing
this and actually utilize her faceless assassin

00:21:31.159 --> 00:21:32.159
skills.

00:21:32.159 --> 00:21:35.430
I know Arya in the show also kind of has her
suspicions towards Dany.

00:21:35.430 --> 00:21:39.480
So whoever survives on Dany’s side like
Missendei or something, could make for an

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:40.480
easy target.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:45.600
A great scene could be Arya wearing Greyworms
face and uses it to kill Missendei.

00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:48.470
Which would be taking out two characters with
one stone.

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:52.440
Then another example to drive Dany mad could
be planting evidence and making it seem as

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:55.289
if her closest advisors are actually betraying
her.

00:21:55.289 --> 00:21:58.890
Like maybe forging a letter in Varys’ name
that tells the lords of Westeros that Jon

00:21:58.890 --> 00:21:59.890
is a Targaryen.

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:03.460
There’s a lot of different things you can
do that play into the scheming aspect of the

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:06.150
show that can undermine and drive Dany crazy.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:10.200
And from all of this, she begins her descent
into madness and overall paranoia.

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:15.409
She can’t trust her closest advisors anymore,
her friends that counseled mercy have been

00:22:15.409 --> 00:22:19.120
assassinated, and Jon is slowly but surely
distancing himself from her.

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:23.470
From here, the same events can play out in
the show where Jon eventually kills Dany and

00:22:23.470 --> 00:22:26.490
this means that Littlefinger makes it to the
end of the show.

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:32.260
However, Sansa knows the true evil nature
of Littlefinger and I think a suitable ending

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:35.419
would be for her to betray and kill Littlefinger.

00:22:35.419 --> 00:22:38.770
Similar to the ending of season 7, but done
much better in my opinion.

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:43.020
Maybe a stipulation in Littlefinger helping
Sansa to drive Danearys crazy is that he wants

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:44.220
to marry her.

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:47.429
Which she obviously doesn’t want so she
betrays him.

00:22:47.429 --> 00:22:51.070
Essentially ending her arc of becoming better
at playing the Game of Thrones and using what

00:22:51.070 --> 00:22:53.160
Littlefinger taught her against him.

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:57.279
I think it would be nice if she comes to this
conclusion by herself and wasn’t necessarily

00:22:57.279 --> 00:22:58.610
aided by Bran.

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:02.059
Bran could come to Sansa with the information
that he brought down the wall, but it makes

00:23:02.059 --> 00:23:06.350
for building a stronger and more independent
character if she wasn’t given this information

00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:07.580
on a golden plate.

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:12.809
And I know Bran is kind of a wildcard character
that with his very existence can curbstomp

00:23:12.809 --> 00:23:16.950
Littlefinger out of the show, but I really
like the evil Bran theory in which he knew

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:20.340
what was going to happen but he let it happen
anyways.

00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:24.700
Bran wanted to become the king and create
a prosperous realm, so he allowed all of these

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:27.150
terrible things to happen so he could get
there.

00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:30.600
Which would be my reasoning for Bran not ratting
out Littlefinger right away.

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:34.830
He knew Littlefinger would serve his common
interest, so he allowed him to live.

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:38.230
Unlike the show where Bran steps in because
Littlefinger was about to manipulate Sansa

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:39.620
into killing Arya.

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:43.760
Littlefinger’s death won’t be a major
blunder made on his part that was just insanely

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:47.330
dumb, but a betrayal from someone he never
expected.

00:23:47.330 --> 00:23:51.539
Sansa uses the lust that Littlefinger has
towards her against him.

00:23:51.539 --> 00:23:55.380
So yeah, this is a massive rework for Littlefinger’s
character that I think would be much more

00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:57.340
satisfactory than what we got.

00:23:57.340 --> 00:24:02.429
I know it requires altering the story a bit
and how it’s formatted, but realistically

00:24:02.429 --> 00:24:06.120
if David and Dan still cared about Game of
Thrones, then they wouldn’t have rushed

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:08.060
it with two shortened seasons.

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:12.820
Like it’s wild to me that they did Cersei's
downfall, The Long Night, and the Mad Queen

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:14.810
Arc in 6 episodes.

00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:19.150
That’s purely insane and with this change
to Littlefinger it made sense to fix other

00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:21.740
things that David and Dan also broke.

00:24:21.740 --> 00:24:25.260
Because it would be physically impossible
to give Littlefinger a great arc in the current

00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:26.260
state of the show.

00:24:26.260 --> 00:24:30.210
Sorry this video ballooned in size and hopefully
my pitch for the character was satisfactory.

00:24:30.210 --> 00:24:34.940
I’d love to go more in depth about it, but
this video would become 40 minutes long probably.

00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:38.720
Thank you for watching and my Letterboxd,
Patreon, and Discord link are in the description.

00:24:38.720 --> 00:24:41.510
And if you made it to this point then you
may as well subscribe.

